                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "The files affected are evident in the diff itself. Please try to avoid listing them in the commit message. Rather, talk about the motivations for doing what you're doing (the \"why\").\n\nBroadly, the guidelines from Linux are battle-tested and worth reading:\n\nhttps://docs.kernel.org/process/submitting-patches.html#describe-your-changes"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Please write in the imperative mood. It's not necessary to say \"This commit\" - the commit message provides that context already.\n\n> Describe your changes in imperative mood, e.g. \u201cmake xyzzy do frotz\u201d instead of \u201c[This patch] makes xyzzy do frotz\u201d or \u201c[I] changed xyzzy to do frotz\u201d, as if you are giving orders to the codebase to change its behaviour.\n\nhttps://docs.kernel.org/process/submitting-patches.html#describe-your-changes"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JINO ABRAHAM",
                        "email": "jinoabraham26@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Jino26"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
